  "notes": [
    "Irregular -ER verb — the *c* changes to *zc* before *o* and *a*: irregular only in the yo form of Presente (*nazco*, not *naco*) and throughout Subjuntivo Presente (*nazca, nazcas...*). All other tenses are fully regular.",
    "This is the same pattern as other -cer/-cir verbs like *conocer* and *parecer*",
    "Past participle: *nacido* (regular)",
    "Almost always used in 3rd person, since it describes people, animals, or things coming into being — *nació en Madrid* (he/she was born in Madrid)",
    "Related: *nacimiento* (birth), *nacional* (national — same root), *renacer* (to be reborn)"
  ],
